      "mergeID": "66bb67e06b5c08418e5432ad",
      "mergedPostDetails": "1. Launch VRChat for iOS Beta.\n\n2. Launch a World. In this case, I tried SupersonicPrivateJet by Moffco.\n\n3. When opening the Quick Menu and then into the Main Menu, the screen will auto-rotate but will cause Screen Tears on the UI.\n\nIn many cases, it will happen all the time when you rotate your Device after launching a game.\n\nTo note, this is the first thing I noticed right as I logged in to the App for the first time. Therefore, I am unable to change my Avatar to one that was compatible with iOS. It’s incredibly difficult to navigate.\n\nDevice Specs:\n\n- iPhone 15 Pro Max\n\n- iOS 17.6.1\n\n- Network: AT&T 5G Cellular\n\nExpected Behavior: The UI should automatically re-draw itself after the device is rotated.\n\nHere’s a video screen recording of it, due to it exceeding Canny’s upload size limit: https://youtube.com/shorts/jduBu7KH4R0?si=WQjm2da1vi3nU_tS",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[2024.2.3] UI Tearing Issues on iOS.",
